WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.760
SCP-682 Vs a Fighter Jet: Who would win?

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.480
Well, that depends on your definition of “win.”

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.600
In terms of short-term immobilization required
for getting 682 recontained, a fighter jet

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.720
would likely be an asset to any MTF hoping
to get 682 back under control, given its high

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.560
speed and weapons capable of at least effectively
stalling the monster.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.800
However, if we’re talking “to the death”
then we’ll have to consider that missiles

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.880
and conventional arms fire have no lasting
effect against 682.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.280
Given enough time, it would adapt to either
fly or fling projectiles capable of taking

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.360
the jet down or BOTH?!

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.600
Imagine a flying, missile-launching 682?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.040
WOW that’s absolutely terrifying.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.360
SCP-682 vs an M1 Abrams Tank: Who would win?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.240
While the M1 Abrams is an enduring piece of
military technology with strong offensive

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.240
and defensive capabilities, is there actually
a contest to be had here?

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.000
682 has survived everything from the Shy Guy
to the Gate Guardian.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.360
The only thing that a tank would offer is
a slightly longer time spent unboxing 682’s

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.120
meal - That being, the unfortunate operatives
running the tank.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.640
The moral of today’s short?

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.600
Don’t bring a tank to an immortal anomaly
fight.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.600
SCP-682 Vs SCP-106.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.240
Reptile Vs Old Man.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.680
The most hateful SCP Vs The Most Sadistic.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.720
Who would win?

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.280
This is another one we have precedent for.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.280
These two engaged in a three-way battle with
SCP-953, the polymorphic humanoid, during

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.560
a containment breach.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.440
All three were pulled into 106’s pocket
dimension, and the battle took place there.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.240
Both returned from the pocket dimension, heavily
injured, and were either easily subdued or

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.120
returned organically to their containment
chambers.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.720
It was a draw.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.040
We can’t imagine either of them would be
eager for a rematch any time soon.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.600
SCP-682 Vs SCP-053.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:00.240
What happens when you pit the Hard to Destroy
Reptile against a very lonely, very deadly

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.120
little girl?

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.080
This Foundation cross-test allowed us to find
out.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:09.360
053 has the power to turn people into violent
maniacs, who then immediately die when they

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:10.640
try to attack her.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.640
Researchers hoped the same thing would happen
to SCP-682.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.880
In fact, the absolute opposite happened.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.400
053 seemed to be one of the only creatures
in the universe that 682 becomes totally docile

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.040
around.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.160
And despite 053’s initial fear of the beast,
she soon plucked up the courage to approach

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.280
and make a friend.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.560
The two played together, with 682 even allowing
053 to draw on its face.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.040
Both became distressed when the two separated.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.840
053 began to cry, and 682 went berserk and
started killing people.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.080
Sadly for both of them, the Foundation has
deemed shared containment to be too much of

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.160
a risk to ever be allowed.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.000
SCP-682 Vs SCP-662.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.080
Can the world’s greatest butler transfer
his skills into being the world’s best monster

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.440
slayer, and finally bring an end to SCP-682?

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.440
When asked to kill the beast, he apologized
profusely and stated that he couldn’t do

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:03.680
it.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.000
He could perhaps distract 682 by sacrificing
himself to it, at least.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.480
As the Foundation persisted&nbsp;
with their questioning,&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.360
Mr. Deeds made an alternate suggestion: Perhaps

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.840
if his body was laced with a powerful toxin
or booby-trapped with explosives, then fed

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.040
to SCP-682, he could do more damage.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.000
Mr. Deeds was dismissed shortly thereafter.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.680
SCP-682 Vs SCP-061.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.840
Could a mind-controlling music program finally
be the key to destroying the infamous Hard

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.040
to Destroy Reptile?

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.600
682 entered the relaxed state typical of people&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.800
undergoing 061 hypnosis at&nbsp;
first, as the Foundation

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.680
gave a number of menial orders, such as rolling
over.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.440
682 clearly tried to resist, even entering
a violent seizure.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:50.240
When ordered to “stand up”, it suddenly
became immune to 061’s powers, carrying

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.360
out a violent assault on the staff and breaching
containment.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.560
It appeared to somehow integrate the abilities
of 061 into its own biology, releasing a screech

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.040
that stunned everyone nearby, and allowing
it to devour several people before it was

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.240
recontained.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.920
SCP-682 Vs SCP-524.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.880
The Hard to Destroy Reptile Vs The cuddly
wittle bunny named Walter that can eat pretty

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:13.920
much everything.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.320
Does 682 look enough like a big, angry carrot
for Walter to get the job done?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.080
682 regarded Walter with suspicion as the
bunny approached.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.040
It then began gnawing through 682’s leg,
causing the giant monster to bellow and flee.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:32.400
He chased 682 around the containment chamber
for several minutes, before 682 tapped out.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.800
682 climbed up the wall of the test chamber
and waited, while Walter washed his face with

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:41.360
his paws. 524 then began chewing his way through
the wall of the test chamber, at which point,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.040
the experiment was aborted.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.000
Still, very good try, little buddy.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.760
SCP-682 Vs SCP-513.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:56.480
Sometimes, to take down a scary SCP like SCP-682,
you need to bring in an even scarier SCP,

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.920
like this demonic cowbell and the phantom
it reveals.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:05.600
SCP-682 was partially incinerated and brought
into a testing chamber, where a robot arm

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:11.280
rang the SCP-513 bell several times, with
the resulting sound causing extreme stress

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.200
for SCP-682.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.480
Aerosolized tranquilizers and sedatives were
pumped into the chamber, causing 682 to fall

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.440
unconscious.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.840
It then began sleepwalking, breaching the
containment chamber, but it wasn’t alone:

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.640
A nightmarish, ghost-like entity, resembling
SCP-682, began stalking the halls.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.680
After mass hysteria and mass staff death across
the site, the Foundation finally got things

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.800
back under control.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:40.400
When SCP-682 was woken up, it complained,
saying that it was having such a lovely dream...

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:48.800
SCP-2305-A: An anomalous document that manifests
methods of neutralizing various SCPs, all

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.640
of which are doomed to fail.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.080
So what did it have to say about SCP-682?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.200
To make a very long and elaborate story short,
through a mix of anomalies and massive hydrogen

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:04.960
bombs, SCP-682 would be transported to the
moon and blown to smithereens in a massive,

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.720
ridiculous explosion.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.080
Earth is pounded by the resulting meteors
from the explosion.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.920
While only a tiny quantity of 682’s blood
survived the bombardment, it managed to regenerate

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:16.800
and adapt.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.640
It became the size of Saturn and ended up
eating our solar system.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.240
The moral of the story: Don’t redacted with
this gecko.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.720
SCP-682 Vs SCP-2521.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.920
An unspeakably cruel and violent reptile Vs
a monster that is literally unspeakable.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:34.640
Who won?

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:35.680
Let’s find out.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:41.200
The Foundation used a laser cutting tool to
etch information about SCP-2521 into the skin

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:47.920
of SCP-682’s side, in the hopes that the
monster would turn up and steal SCP-682.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.400
However, it didn’t work out that way.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.520
Instead, it just appeared and tore the skin
off of 682’s side before demanifesting.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.400
682 regenerated the missing skin later.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.600
Better luck next time.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.720
Oh, come on!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.840
Every time!

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:07.280
SCP-682 Vs SCP-811.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.600
Could the sweet, misunderstood Swamp Woman
finally end the wretched life of the Hard

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.800
to Destroy Reptile?

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:13.840
Let’s find out.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.960
In a rare act of cross-test kindness, the
Foundation refused to pit 811 against 682

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.360
directly, due to the justifiable fear that
it would simply murder the Swamp Woman.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.640
However, the Swamp Woman’s deadly, corrosive
mucus was harvested and applied to 682’s

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:29.280
skin.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:35.040
The fizzling muck was able to reduce 682’s
body mass by 27%, until the creature evolved

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.920
a complete bone covering of the remaining
body mass, rendering the mucus ineffective.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:44.880
But hey, at least this didn’t cause any
undue stress to SCP-811.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.520
SCP-682 Vs SCP-2578-D.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.400
The Hard to Destroy Reptile would kill millions
if ever it was allowed to escape and be free.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:08:00.000
Would the SCP-2578-D Impaler spacecraft be
able to put its reign of terror to an end?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.800
SCP-2578-D is a mysterious spacecraft with
an immensely powerful and precise proton cannon.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:12.000
It seeks to protect democracy and human rights
from tyrants, fascists, and authoritarians

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.360
through controlled assassinations, or “Impaler
Events.”

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.400
One such event befell 682 in containment,
with five cranial penetrative wounds that

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:25.040
pierced its skull during a brief period, leaving
it out of commission for 32 minutes.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.880
It then woke back up and yelled “F YOU AND
ALL THREE OF YOUR MOONS!”

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.480
up to the ceiling.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.800
The spacecraft later sent an email to the
Foundation, apologizing that it hadn’t killed

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.840
682.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.280
In its defense, though, it hadn’t missed
a single shot.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:43.760
SCP-682 Vs SCP-2337.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:47.520
Could the Hard to Destroy Reptile meet its
end at the dangerously booming voice of the

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.120
talkative Dr. Spanko?

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:54.320
As part of a tissue test, Dr. Spanko was told
682’s flesh was a tone-deaf food critic

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.240
who needed to be convinced on what the greatest
food in existence was.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:04.400
Spanko argued so loudly that the answer was
gummy worms that it destroyed 682’s flesh.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.120
The next step was sending him in to talk the
actual 682 to death, after being told the

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.240
reptile was an “anti-gummy worm extremist.”

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:17.520
This seemed promising until Dr. Spanko confidently
entered the chamber, and 682 simply boomed

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:23.120
“LEAVE”, at which point Dr. Spanko turned,
literally yelled the wall down, and did just

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:23.680
that.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.240
682 must really hate gummy worms.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:30.800
SCP-682 Vs SCP-2617.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.720
Could the icy operatives of the winter command
finally be the ones to take down the Hard

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.000
to Destroy Reptile?

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:42.880
SCP-682 was airlifted into the abandoned Russian
village where the 2617 radio tower was situated,

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:47.520
and the Foundation fed the tower the reptile’s
coordinates as it began attacking the village.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:54.320
2617 generated a large number of deadly ice
warriors, who took on SCP-682 with both ferocity

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.880
and skill, destroying 45% of its body mass
through sustained attacks.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.440
It looked like they might have the lizard
on the ropes…

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:08.320
Until it began putting out its own radio waves,
affecting and disrupting the 2617 radio tower,

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.640
as well as the researchers in attendance.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:16.160
The affected personnel, when later interviewed,
were unable to recognize even the concept

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:16.800
of Russia.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.880
SCP-682 Vs SCP-3930.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.760
Could the patch of nothingness, the true oblivion
in the heart of rural Russia, finally consign

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.240
the nightmarish reptile to non-existence?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.040
Let’s see.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:34.400
The tissue sample from 682 was successfully
destroyed by being placed inside 3930.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.680
But the rest of the reptile would be a little
more complicated.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.880
Its body was placed into the void and ceased
existing.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.360
However, despite ceasing to exist, it could
still be perceived and slaughtered several

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.840
of the guards and researchers in attendance.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.080
Thankfully, it did eventually disappear.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:55.360
Until 15 hours later, when it suddenly manifested
once again in its containment chamber, good

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.080
as new.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.200
Of course, nobody really knows how or why.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.600
We just don’t question it at this point.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.840
SCP-682 Vs SCP-1056.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:10.960
Could this anomalous, body-warping kitchen
timer finally be the thing that shrinks SCP-682

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:11.840
down to size?

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:12.880
Let’s find out.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:18.080
The objective of the test was to see how long
it would take SCP-682 to return to its normal

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:22.240
size after being resized by SCP-1056.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:26.240
However, when the creature was meant to be
shrunk to a quarter of its size, it simply

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.040
disappeared.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:32.240
It was later found causing chaos outside of
Site-19, having returned to its normal size.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.680
When a Mobile Task Force was sent to apprehend
682, it released a wave that instead massively

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.040
shrunk the task force.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.840
It continued to rampage elsewhere, manipulating
its size at will, until a combined group of

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:46.800
Mobile Task Forces were able to incapacitate
it.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:52.480
Researchers concluded that it had not only
absorbed the anomalous effect of SCP-1056,

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:58.640
but enhanced it, leading to considerably more
powerful defensive and offensive body-resizing

00:11:58.640 --> 00:11:59.600
capabilities.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.480
SCP-682 Vs SCP-3207.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:09.840
No weapon the Foundation has ever created
has been able to kill SCP-682, so maybe a

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:15.280
crazy anomalous energy cannon created by Leonardo
Davinci and Marco Saul will get the job done.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:20.720
The tissue test went well, as the energy cannon
was able to completely vaporize the SCP-682

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.400
flesh with a single blast.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:27.680
With this promising result, they went on to
the full test: 3207 appeared to completely

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:33.760
annihilate SCP-682 with a few well-aimed blasts,
leading to a great deal of relief among the

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:35.360
attending researchers…

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:37.200
For a few hours, at least.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:42.160
Several nasty little creatures regenerated
from the scattered tissue of SCP-682.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:47.040
When these creatures breached containment,
they fused back into SCP-682.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.440
Because of course they did.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.200
SCP-682 Vs SCP-393.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:58.160
So many of the Foundation’s plans to kill
SCP-682 have failed, but maybe that’s just

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:03.920
because they never wrote it down in SCP-393,
this singularly unique day planner.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:09.520
SCP-393 is a day planner that bonds to a nearby
subject, and when they write their plans into

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:13.840
it, they will soon develop a complete memory
of having achieved those plans.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.200
Perhaps this could be used to figure out how
to kill 682.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:22.640
A D-Class was given the planner, and asked
to write “Going to somehow defeat SCP-682

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:23.200
today.”

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:27.360
The D-Class was later found comatose with
a horrified expression on their face, and

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.720
died shortly after.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:33.600
A defeated note from a young research assistant
on the test file reads, “It was worth a

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:34.320
shot…”

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:39.280
SCP-682 VS An Industrial-Grade Blender Followed
by Strong Centrifuge.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:43.440
Could this, the most hardcore of industrial
kitchen equipment, finally take down the Hard

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.480
to Destroy Reptile?

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:49.680
A 682 tissue sample was reduced into a fine
slurry by the blender and then placed into

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:54.800
the centrifuge, which slowly increased to
a truly insane number of rotations per minute.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:55.440
And…

00:13:55.440 --> 00:14:00.160
The sample exploded, severely injuring twelve
members of personnel and almost killing Dr.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.960
Carlson, one of the lead researchers on the
project.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:08.400
It turned out that SCP-682’s flesh contains
anti-matter, hence the violent chemical reaction

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:09.600
that transpired.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:13.840
Naturally, further testing of this matter
was forbidden by the O5 Council, to reduce

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.960
the number of unnecessary explosions occurring
on site.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:20.240
I guess we’ll never truly know the outcome
on this one huh?

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:27.040
SCP-682, the indestructible reptile, versus
SCP-241, “Good Home Cooking”.

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:29.440
What happens when you&nbsp;
introduce the humanity-hating&nbsp;

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.440
lizard to a cookbook that sends the person

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.920
eating the recipes into anaphylactic shock?

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:34.880
Let’s find out.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:39.520
A portion of 682’s skin tissue was fixed
to a steel rod, which was held by a D-Class

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.840
and used to turn the pages of 241.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:47.040
The cookbook displayed 99 new recipes, including
three in an unknown language, two that were

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:50.720
completely incomprehensible, and one that
contained a memetic kill agent.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:55.440
The remaining recipes all contained instructions
that made accurate preparation impossible,

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.640
such as “marinate for 900 trillion years”.

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:02.080
D-Class personnel was tasked with preparing
these 93 recipes.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.600
Upon completion, each dish was served directly
to the lizard.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:09.840
Naturally, it was able to consume all 93 meals
without any difficulty.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:14.560
For 682, this was most likely one of the more
enjoyable termination attempts.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.760
Bon appétit!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.880
SCP-682, the indestructible reptile, versus&nbsp;

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:22.960
SCP-3519, a dangerous&nbsp;
memetic contagion responsible

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.680
for killing nearly the entire population of
the world.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:31.200
In a certain timeline, SCP-3519 infected global
media to influence the public into believing

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.894
that the world would end on March 5th, 2019,
and that self-destruction was a preferable

00:15:33.894 --> 00:15:33.917
option.

00:15:33.917 --> 00:15:37.680
Weeks before March 5th, a group of Foundation
personnel decided to test 3519’s exposure

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:41.600
with 682, in hopes that it may terminate the
lizard once and for all.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:46.400
Lowering the acid levels inside its tank,
682 was exposed to the contagion, but did

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:48.640
not show any self-destructive ideation.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:52.160
Instead, 682 nightmarishly laughed for 193&nbsp;

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:54.640
seconds before it was placed&nbsp;
back into containment.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:16:00.000
After March 5th, there was only one lone human
survivor, Junior Researcher Dr. Rory Jones.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.240
When 682 encountered the Doctor after breaching
containment, it did not kill him.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:07.920
Instead, it simply stated:
“We are alike now, meat.

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:10.640
Killing you would only end suffering"

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:17.440
SCP-682, the indestructible reptile, versus
SCP-1237, the epsilon wave, who would win?

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:17.680
In an attempt to terminate SCP-682, the Foundation
gave us the answer.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:23.120
SCP-1237 is a brain pattern occurring in deep
REM sleep that allows an individual's dreams

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.280
to shape and affect reality when they wake.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:31.760
One specimen affected by SCP-1237 was permitted
to observe SCP-682 and was instructed to dream

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:37.280
that SCP-682 was a small house cat with no
anomalous abilities, and that the Foundation

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.120
had successfully terminated it.

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:43.120
Seven seconds into their sleep, the subject
seized violently and died less than a minute

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:46.240
later, alongside 13 other observing security
personnel.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:50.320
Their bodies were covered with scratches and
bites, as well as symptoms of toxoplasmosis

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:51.600
and bubonic plague.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:56.640
Inside SCP-682’s chamber was a small house
cat, licking blood from its coat of fur.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.480
It regenerated into SCP-682 only a few hours
later.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:05.040
Looks like in this matchup, the lizard, not
the cat, got the foundation’s tongue, as

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.080
expected.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:09.120
SCP-682 Vs a Vacuum.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:12.080
And we’re not talking about the household
cleaning appliance.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:15.760
Could the Hard to Destroy Reptile survive
in a completely air-free environment?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:21.520
To find out, 99% of the oxygen was removed
from a testing chamber that SCP-682 was trapped

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:22.160
inside.

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:26.160
The creature entered a dormant state, and
began producing what the Foundation believed

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:33.680
to be its native atmosphere - A mixture of
56% ozone, 23% chlorine, 18% xenon, and other

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:34.880
caustic elements.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.480
The test was eventually called to an end,
however, when our normal earth atmosphere

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:43.200
was reintroduced into the room, it reacted
with the compound that 682 was releasing,

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:46.480
and caused a massive explosion that blew off
the blast door.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:51.680
A scientist remarked that it was no wonder
682 was so hardy if that poisonous mix was

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.040
its native atmosphere.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:57.200
SCP-682 Vs Y-909.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:02.400
Can the compound derived from SCP-3000, the
legendary Ananatashesha, be the thing that

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.760
finally ends the wretched life of SCP-682?

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:10.240
Y-909 is the key ingredient in Foundation
amnestics, and the researchers discovered

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:15.120
a curious thing when it was added to 682’s
tank: It caused an increase in the damage

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.920
that hydrochloric acid did to the creature’s
body.

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:23.040
This suggested that 682’s regenerative abilities
are somehow tied to its memories of previous

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.160
damage taken.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:30.800
Some researchers proposed taking SCP-682 directly
to SCP-3000, to see if the giant eel could

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:32.880
kill 682 once and for all.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:37.840
However, this proposal was soundly rejected,
due to too many unpredictable factors: From

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:43.535
the risk of transporting 682, to its unpredictable
adaptive response to SCP-3000, such as it

00:18:43.535 --> 00:18:48.720
possibly growing to SCP-3000’s insane size
or stealing its amnestic abilities.

